# Fixing Metadata

Apply this rule when changing page titles, descriptions, canonical URLs, robots directives, Open Graph tags, Twitter cards, favicons, app icons, manifests, theme color, JSON-LD structured data, locale metadata, deployment URLs, path prefixes, or new public pages.

## Workflow

1. Identify the project metadata source of truth: shared layout, `src/_data/site.json`, page front matter, or an existing SEO component.
2. Identify every affected generated page and its final public URL.
3. Build before validation when generated HTML is involved. Do not hand-edit `dist/`.
4. Check for duplicate or conflicting `<title>`, description, canonical, robots, Open Graph, and Twitter tags.
5. Ensure title, description, canonical URL, `og:url`, deployment URL, trailing slash, and path-prefix behavior agree.
6. Ensure public shareable pages have safe defaults and page-specific overrides where useful.
7. Use absolute public URLs for social images.
8. Add JSON-LD only when it truthfully matches visible page content.
9. Verify social cards on a real deployed URL when possible; localhost is not enough.
10. Keep diffs scoped to metadata unless broader SEO/content work is explicitly requested.

## Eleventy Pattern

- Store global defaults in `src/_data/site.json` when the project already uses site data.
- Store page-specific metadata in front matter, for example `title`, `description`, `image`, `canonical`, `robots`, or `ogType`.
- Render metadata in the shared base layout.
- Use existing Eleventy URL/path-prefix conventions.
- Inspect generated `dist/**/*.html` after `npm run build`.

## Review Priorities

- Critical: duplicate/conflicting metadata, unstable values, public pages accidentally noindexed, canonical/indexing contradictions.
- High: missing title/description/canonical on public pages, `og:url` mismatch, missing social basics for shareable pages.
- Medium: missing favicon/app icon/theme-color, weak social image dimensions, JSON-LD mismatch, missing locale metadata.
- Low: title format polish, optional manifest improvements, non-critical social preview copy.

## Boundaries

- Do not add SEO/head libraries unless explicitly requested or already standard in the project.
- Do not introduce a second metadata system.
- Do not invent JSON-LD facts, ratings, offers, organization details, or contact data.
- Do not refactor unrelated templates, styles, scripts, or content.
- Preserve Figma-first and validation-playbook workflows when metadata work is part of a larger page task.
